    <documentation>pm:Stack of `merge-pt-member`. This document shows how the stack's layers and operations connect, and none of its figures. How much of the system the stack holds is stated on the laneSet. [assets/sqlc/diagrams/pools.sqlc]</documentation>
    <laneSet id="lanes_merge-pt-member" name="draw">
      <documentation>scope: unbounded. `complete` says there are no other layers of this system, `scoped` says somebody established what lies outside and left it out, `unbounded` says nobody looked. A lane set has no way to say which, so this sentence is the only place it is said. The filing's reason: o que este membro reporta ao abrigo da instrução do grupo, e ninguém perguntou o que fica fora disso [assets/sqlc/diagrams/scopes.sqlc]</documentation>
      <documentation>coupling search: unmeasured. `unmeasured` means nobody looked, `none` means somebody looked and found no dependence, `notApplicable` means there is no pair to couple, and `stated` means the dependences drawn here. An absent line is not independence. [assets/sqlc/diagrams/searches.sqlc]</documentation>
      <lane id="lane_merge-pt-member_capacidade-instalada" name="capacidade-instalada">
        <documentation>rank 0: the number of levels of parts beneath this layer. At 0 it waits on nothing; above 0 it waits for every part below it to arrive [assets/sqlc/rank/evaluation_order.sqlc]</documentation>
      </lane>
      <lane id="lane_merge-pt-member_compute" name="compute">
        <documentation>rank 0: the number of levels of parts beneath this layer. At 0 it waits on nothing; above 0 it waits for every part below it to arrive [assets/sqlc/rank/evaluation_order.sqlc]</documentation>
